@startuml eof-questionnaire-sequence-p3
title EOF questionnaire - Page 3/3 : read back, merge, redo the report

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #E0F0F4
  BorderColor #5BA1BC
  FontColor #1C2856
}
skinparam actor {
  BackgroundColor #E0F0F4
  BorderColor #5BA1BC
  FontColor #1C2856
}
skinparam ArrowColor #5BA1BC
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #5BA1BC
skinparam SequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor #ECECF2
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #5BA1BC
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #E0F0F4
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9BD0DD
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 200
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Auditor" as U #82C1DD
participant "Claude\n(skill analyse-parcours)" as C #82C1DD
participant "parse_questionnaire.py" as PQ #DBDDE5
participant "merge_lots.py" as FL #DBDDE5
participant "generate_report_html.py" as GR #DBDDE5
database "audit-dir/" as FS #9BD0DD

== Read back the ticked boxes ==

U -> C : Request the read-back
C -> PQ : python3 parse_questionnaire.py <audit-dir>
PQ -> FS : Read the filled-in questionnaire-eof.md
FS -> PQ : Ticked boxes
PQ -> PQ : Navigate on the HTML comments,\nnever on a line number
PQ -> FS : lots/questionnaire-review.json\n+ a measurement block saying whether the file was there

note over PQ, FS
  Provenance set on these answers: "stated",
  i.e. a box ticked by the audited service,
  without attached proof.
  An "I don't know" box never becomes an
  answer: it stays a simple comment.
end note

== Merge the measured and the declared ==

C -> FL : python3 merge_lots.py <audit-dir>
FL -> FS : Read all lots/*.json
FS -> FL : Automatic judgment\n+ questionnaire read-back
FL -> FL : Apply the precedence:\ncollected > estimated > stated > declared > assumed

note over FL, FS
  What the precedence guarantees:
  a value we measured ourselves can
  never be overwritten by a declaration.
  But a box ticked by the client comes BEFORE a
  deduction we would make from a weak signal:
  the client knows their team, we guess.
end note

alt Two lots contradict at equal provenance
  FL -> C : Refuse to merge, error exit
else Divergence between different provenances
  FL -> FS : The highest provenance wins,\nthe discrepancy is recorded in the context
end

FL -> FS : eof-audit-results.json\n(rewritten: measured + declared)
FL -> FS : eof-radar-<domain>.svg\n(regenerated, 2 layers)

== Redo the report ==

C -> GR : python3 generate_report_html.py <audit-dir>
GR -> FS : Read eof-audit-results.json\n+ the regenerated radar
GR -> FS : journey-report-YYYY-MM-DD.html
C -> U : Report enriched with the answers\nof the audited service's team

note over U, FS
  TRAP. THE MANIPULATION TRAP TO KNOW.
  run_eof.py rewrites eof-audit-results.json without re-reading
  the lots. Rerunning it alone therefore makes all the
  questionnaire answers disappear from the
  report, silently. Always rerun merge_lots.py
  after run_eof.py.
end note

@enduml
